The Arch Linux mirrorlist is located at /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist and defines
sources from which pacman will download packages. Generally speaking, mirrors
located closer to you will offer better download speeds. For this reason, it is
recommended to edit the mirrorlist before bootstrapping the system as this will
speed up the downloading of packages. Additionally, the mirrorlist on the live
medium will be copied over to the new system.

Each line in /etc/pacman.d/mirrorlist is either the address of a pacman mirror
or a comment prefixed with #. Mirrors are listed in decending priority. The
mirrorlist on the live medium is usually grouped into countries making it easy
to identify mirrors closer to you. However, as this organization is not
guaranteed, we will open the mirrorlist directly so you can manually edit it to
suit your needs.

